## Summary

Renamed the two C-style types to PascalCase (`hash_item` → `HashItem`, `hash_table` → `HashTable`), removed the now-unneeded `#[allow(non_camel_case_types)]` lint allowances, and folded the six free functions that took a `&mut hash_table` first argument (`hash_create`, `hash_create_ex`, `hash_retrieve`, `hash_insert`, `hash_delete_item`, `hash_delete_key`) into inherent methods on `HashTable` — the constructors became `HashTable::new` / `HashTable::with_seed`, and the rest dropped their `hash_` prefix and switched to `&mut self`. Per the error-model rule, the two constructors now return `Result<Box<Self>, Error>` (mapping C's `NULL` to `Error::Memory`) instead of `Option<Box<…>>`. Refreshed the module-level and per-item docs to reference Rust names rather than C identifiers and to drop low-value line-number-anchored cross-references; kept `// C: picohash_*` traceability notes and the freestanding `hash_bytes` / `hash_siphash` helpers (they don't take a table). Propagated the type renames to the only caller, `internal.rs` (the `use` line, four embedded-`HashItem` fields on `cnx_t` / `path_t` / `local_cnxid_t` / `issued_ticket_t`, and the five `*mut HashTable` fields on `quic_t`). `cargo check` and `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` both clean.


